{"name":"Zucchini Noodles","hex":"#c8d07f","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"zucchini","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A courgette; a variety of squash, Cucurbita pepo, which bears edible fruit.","The edible fruit of this variety of squash."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of zucchino"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/zucchini"},{"term":"noodles","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of noodle"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Euphemistic form of nudes (“nude photographs”).","Redstone circuitry."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/noodles"}],"entries":[{"title":"Spiral vegetable slicer","blocks":[{"text":"Spiral vegetable slicers are kitchen appliances used for cutting vegetables, such as zucchinis, potatoes, cucumbers, carrots, apples, parsnips, and beetroots, into linguine-like strands which can be used as an alternative to pasta."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/The_spiralizer_in_action%21_%284617278380%29.jpg/330px-The_spiralizer_in_action%21_%284617278380%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spiral_vegetable_slicer"},{"title":"Zucchini","blocks":[{"text":"Zucchini, courgette, or Cucurbita pepo var. cylindrica is a summer squash, a vining herbaceous plant whose fruit are harvested when their immature seeds and epicarp (rind) are still soft and edible. It is closely related, but not identical, to the marrow; its fruit may be called marrow when mature."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/CSA-Striped-Zucchini.jpg/330px-CSA-Striped-Zucchini.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zucchini"},{"title":"Noodles","blocks":[{"text":"Noodles are a type of food typically made from unleavened dough which is rolled flat and cut, stretched, or extruded into long strips or strings. Noodles are a staple food in many cultures and made into a variety of shapes. The most common noodles are those derived from Chinese cuisine or Italian cuisine. Italian noodles are generally referred to as pasta. In Chinese cuisine, the overarching term for noodles is 麵, which refers specifically to dough-based noodles made from wheat or other grain-based dough. Chinese noodles also include another category, called 粉 (fěn), which are not made by kneading dough but from a starch slurry, such as rice noodles, and cellophane noodles. These are not made from wheat dough, but are still regarded as noodles in English due to their physical form and culinary role."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/Dalian_Liaoning_China_Noodlemaker-01.jpg/330px-Dalian_Liaoning_China_Noodlemaker-01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Noodles"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Zucchini_noodles_%28spiral_slicer%29.jpg/500px-Zucchini_noodles_%28spiral_slicer%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Zucchini_noodles_%28spiral_slicer%29.jpg/1280px-Zucchini_noodles_%28spiral_slicer%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Zucchini_noodles_%28spiral_slicer%29.jpg/500px-Zucchini_noodles_%28spiral_slicer%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AZucchini_noodles_(spiral_slicer).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Zucchini-Whole.jpg/500px-Zucchini-Whole.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7c/Zucchini-Whole.jpg/1280px-Zucchini-